  "name": "Sıra gecesi (Şanlıurfa gathering music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the sıra gecesi, evening gatherings of men held in rotation in the homes of Şanlıurfa in southeastern Turkey, where friends share food and conversation and take turns singing the city's türkü, hoyrat and gazel in its own makam-based style with a small ensemble of local musicians. The gatherings are among the Traditional Sohbet meetings inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage.",
  "recipe": "classic modern sıra gecesi, ballad Poetry, med east poetic branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. oud, kanun tortoiseshell traditional kanun, clay pre modern traditional darbuka. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
